hw/sh4: ze0 SCIF channels as named host chardevs with receive (TODO M8.H1).

Every SCIF 0-8 gets a machine property sciN=<chardev id>.  With a chardev,
sh_serial carries TX to the host and RX from it into the FIFO; without one
the old stub behaviour (TX into the void) is kept.  The HPB-DMAC channels
armed from a SCIF FRDR drain that FIFO into the guest buffers and complete,
so a host peer can answer the frames of EXP-2026-11-22-M8.C2a-serial-dma.

run.sh --serial-peer sciN=unix:PATH creates the chardev and the property.
